{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They bent</b> [רשת, כפף] — a verb standing in masculine form like כל נפש שבעה (every living creature was destroyed), or it may be a transitive [verb], and the meaning is: each one bent my soul." "<b>A pit</b> [שיחה] — like שוחה קריאי (the pit of those who call), like קרואי, and likewise שישיחו, those who fell within it in truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {1 "The comparison terms (שוחה קריאי / קרואי / שישיחו) are obscure; translated hyper-literally as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:06.680036646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}